<title>ITALY: Prodi says Italy lira exchange rate &quot;makes sense&quot;.</title>
<headline>Prodi says Italy lira exchange rate &quot;makes sense&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Tuesday the Italian lira's exchange rate was sensible.</p>
<p>&quot;We have an exchange rate which seems to me to make sense,&quot; he told foreign journalists in Rome.</p>
<p>The lira was trading at around 977.35 to the German mark at 1525 GMT on Tuesday, above the central parity of 990 to the mark at which it was readmitted to Europe's exchange rate mechanism (ERM) last November.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
